From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 21:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: order passthrough resume after callback seeks

A resume callback can seek synchronously after the old speed path has already
released audio/video. Keep eligible seekable-file passthrough A/V playback
paused while tracked callbacks execute, servicing the player queue throughout.
Follow completion with a normal-priority FIFO barrier. Preserve any callback
seek's buffering state when committing the requested speed.

Keep request identity stable through seeks while invalidating output identity.
Cancel on pause, overriding speed, stop and replacement playback; stale barriers
cannot release a replacement request. A failed or timed-out callback uses a
logged ordinary-resume fallback without repeating the notification. The timeout
is checked when the player loop runs, not a hard deadline over blocking I/O.

Queue pause/resume notifications in request order. Serialize desired-speed
publication with request insertion so rapid toggles retain the latest intent,
and compare speed requests in matching units to avoid duplicate normal resumes.
No callback or endpoint action runs under that request lock.

This is generic Kodi player/callback ordering, which cannot be implemented by
an AML sink or renderer: only VideoPlayer owns the speed and seek queue. No
platform dependency or additional addon is introduced. It does not establish
hardware presentation hold, decoder readiness or a 500 ms audio lead-in.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
